Scopes
description: the ladder - more colons, wider scope; no implicit search
- >
  A pointer with no leading scope sigil resolves **against the current mapping** - the node that
  contains it: `*cat` is the sibling key `cat`; `*..: x` walks to the parent node, then descends.
  There is **no implicit search up the ancestors** - a bare name is current-mapping only, which avoids
  fragile dynamic-scope capture; reach outward explicitly with `..` or a wider rung of the ladder.
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Form
    - Base
      width: 2
    - Example
  - ['`*name`, `*..: ...`', 'current mapping / its parents', '`*cat`, `*..: ..: pets: 1`']
  - ['`*: ...`', 'current **document** root', '`*: pets: 1`']
  - ['`*:: ...`', 'current **project** root', '`*:: $defs: tag`']
  - ['`*::: auth: ...`', 'the **world** - an identity, never fetched', '`*::: pet.store.com: pets`']
- >
  A **world** base names a project by its authority - a DNS-style `{project}.{company}` name - and
  resolution goes through the local mount table ([names, not
  fetches](*::language:principles:names-not-fetches)). **Imports** are root-level keys whose value is a
  world-scoped link (`yamlover: *::: yamlover.inthemoon.net`); inside a project the self-import is
  absorbed, so `:: $defs: tag` and `:: yamlover: $defs: tag` are the same path.
- 'Formally, a pointer is its scope and its segments:'
- !!<format: text/plain> |
  pointer = scope *( ":" segment )
  scope   = ":::" ws authority   ; the world
          / "::"                 ; current project root
          / ":"                  ; current document root
          / ".."                 ; parent node
          / segment              ; a key / position in the current mapping
  segment = 1*DIGIT              ; bare digits - the position (integer key)
          / "~"                  ; the null key
          / "-"                  ; the keyless segment (bookmark append / query any-position)
          / ( name / ".." ) *( relindex )
          / 1*( relindex )       ; a bare relative position: *[.-1]
